Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.20 Cheats screen hooks (DW3_CHEATS builds only)

The Cheats sub-screen of the Options screen (port/options/cheats.c,
docs/PORT_OPTIONS.md "Cheats") drives the PC test hooks that already exist,
so the cheats reuse their code instead of adding new game logic. Every line
is inside #ifdef DW3_CHEATS (CMake option DW3_CHEATS, default ON): a build
with -DDW3_CHEATS=OFF compiles these files exactly as without this patch.
With it, nothing changes while the Cheats screen's master switch is off.

* Fill bag (field_menu/menu.c): patch 0070's DW3_FORCE_ITEMS hook reads
  dw3_cheats_getenv. The variable still wins when it is set (replays); else
  the armed one-shot answers "43-359:99" once (usable items and equipment, no
  key item) and is used up.
* Instant win (normal_battle/menu.c): the end of patch 0025's DW3_FORCE_WIN
  hook (FIGHTSTG_endBattle(BATTLE_WON) on the battle menu's turn state), once
  in every battle while the toggle is on. FIGHTSTG's start counts battles
  (battle_mode/start.c). With DW3_FORCE_WIN set the variable's hook acts and
  the cheat does not.
* Battle now (field_mode/battle.c): in front of patch 0062's countdown hook,
  while the one-shot is ready the footstep's step is DW3_CHEAT_BATTLE_NOW_STEP
  (more than any countdown), whatever the Encounter rate row says; when the
  random battle starts the one-shot is used up and logged instead of the
  P6.18 footstep line. It stays ready in an area whose random battles are off.
* The save mark (memory_card/saves.c): after a slot is written,
  dw3_cheats_save_written gets the port, the slot, the slot's offset in the
  card file (MEMCARD.offset of the section) and the bytes written; the port
  keeps the mark in save<N>.cheats beside save<N>.bin, never in the save.
  After a slot is loaded, dw3_cheats_save_loaded keeps a marked game marked.
* The title menu's task start (title/menu.c) clears the mark of the game in
  progress: a new game or a load follows.

